                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Are you looking for a physical puzzle game?[/b]\n\nBlok Drop Neo supposed to be one. The goal of this game to keep the orange cube on one of the platforms while you destroy the grey cubes/objects. Sounds easy right? It is actually, all levels solveable in a few tries.\n\n[b]Whats the problem with Blok Drop Neo?[/b]\n\nThere are only 30 levels and you done with the game in less than half hour. The game is too simple, only one new element as you progress in the game, which is the blue cube. The blue cube bounce other cubes. At the better times such games were free on browser game sites, sadly steam nowadays full with these kind of games and they asking money for it and if you ask me a half hour long minimalistic casual game definetly not worth 2,99eur.\n\n[b]Hey, iam an achievement hunter![/b]\n\nSo if you achievement hunter like me then the game still have a purpose! It can increase your perfect game count and your AVGC:-) The game has 1 achievement for completing every level, total of 30 achievements for the 30 levels and you dont need more than 30minutes for this game.\n\n[b]This review was created for Average Achievement Hunter curator[/b]\n\nFollow my curator if you like to see achievement related informations (completion time, difficulty to get all achievements) on store page of the games.\n\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/curator/30168383-Average-Achievement-Hunter/ \n\nThe curator group dont mark any game as recommended so it shows useful information about achievements on the store page of the games without influencing the main store page of steam with recommendations + all games sorted to lists based on expected completion times. No point not to follow!:-)",
